{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789915785,"nonce":"39kjJxi/xaGMxU2Aff5hsQtba3o=","title":"An instance method named bare as a value has no receiver","message":"`var f = inst; f(4)` (also `fn = inst` into a typed local, `a.map(inst)`)\nSIGSEGVs: the Ident lowers to a `FunctionRef` of the closure-value adapter\nwith a null env, and the adapter reads `this` from its first slot.\n`this.inst` and `o.inst` build the bound closure correctly. Fix: in the\nTAST, a bare identifier that names a non-static method of the current\nclass, used as a value (not a call's callee), lowers as `this.\u003cname\u003e`.","files":null}]}